static const char _zs257_d[] = "private escape\n\nA `.private` view may only be taken by the value's own type, or by a holder of an existing `.private` handle (a friend the type passed it to). External code holding only a public value cannot produce one.";
static const z_t79_t _zs257 = { .data = _zs257_d, .size = 220 };
static const char _zs258_d[] = "ownership error\n\nA value's ownership was used incorrectly: used after a take/move, a borrow outliving its lock, a reftype aliased while locked, or a reassignment in another mode than the name was bound with -- an owned name takes an owned value (`x = d.take`), a borrow is re-pointed (`b = d`). See docs/ownership.";
static const z_t79_t _zs258 = { .data = _zs258_d, .size = 314 };
static const char _zs259_d[] = "call error\n\nA call's arguments do not match the callee: wrong count, an unknown named argument, or an argument type mismatch. Also raised for a bare type name in value position that cannot construct its zero value: required fields missing, or a family with no zero-argument create (unions/variants select an arm, views bind from an owner, generic templates need type arguments).";
